WEBVTT

00:03.190 --> 00:04.980
Good grief!

00:04.980 --> 00:08.650
What were you thinking, 
peeking at classified data from HQ?!

00:08.890 --> 00:11.100
I know. I screwed up.

00:11.100 --> 00:13.420
It's Inspector Hosorogi, isn't it?

00:14.120 --> 00:17.050
Don't stick your neck out for someone 
who's no longer with us.

00:17.050 --> 00:18.860
But I can't just—

00:18.860 --> 00:20.870
I'm telling you to face forward.

00:21.320 --> 00:23.330
For those who are gone, and for yourself.

00:26.020 --> 00:27.630
About your daughter...

00:28.240 --> 00:29.230
I'm sorry.

00:29.610 --> 00:31.500
Listen, Iwanome.

00:32.080 --> 00:33.260
I'm alive.

00:34.250 --> 00:35.800
For my daughter, and for me,

00:36.810 --> 00:40.770
I'm going to see my job 
through to the bitter end.

02:18.100 --> 02:20.200
I'm impressed, Habaki-san.

02:20.200 --> 02:24.660
Was all that talk about your 
daughter just a pack of lies?

02:25.590 --> 02:26.790
My daughter?

02:27.250 --> 02:28.870
Of course not!

02:28.870 --> 02:30.250
Wh-Whoa there.

02:30.590 --> 02:33.460
I traded my daughter for this position.

02:33.730 --> 02:35.960
Like hell I'll give it up!

02:36.230 --> 02:37.160
Are you kidding me?!

02:38.340 --> 02:40.800
Try to calm down, boss.

02:43.510 --> 02:46.090
He's still better than Lemmings, right?

02:46.090 --> 02:48.210
Well, you have a point.

02:50.100 --> 02:51.810
Are you okay, Iwa-san?!

02:52.090 --> 02:53.030
Yatsu!

02:54.190 --> 02:56.860
I passed a weird officer, so I got worried.

02:59.020 --> 03:01.160
I rounded up the guys from Comps-3.

03:01.370 --> 03:02.640
Is that a problem?

03:02.640 --> 03:04.870
Nice going, but I'll thank you later!

03:05.830 --> 03:06.590
Whoa!

03:06.590 --> 03:07.790
Oh, my.

03:07.790 --> 03:09.790
S-Senior Commissioner Habaki?!

03:10.860 --> 03:13.060
So, what are the charges, sir?

03:13.060 --> 03:16.500
Thanks for cutting to the chase. 
It's about Hosorogi-san.

03:16.500 --> 03:17.390
Oh?

03:17.390 --> 03:20.220
Maybe I should thank the Fire-Breathing Bug.

03:20.220 --> 03:23.180
Thanks to them, I made it in time.

03:23.930 --> 03:25.950
<i>He's on a call? With who?</i>

03:25.950 --> 03:29.140
<i>That Higuro guy, or someone el—</i>

03:31.600 --> 03:32.440
Arase!

03:32.440 --> 03:33.190
On it!

03:36.900 --> 03:37.740
Great!

03:37.740 --> 03:38.830
Keep it u—

03:40.130 --> 03:40.950
<i>A handgun?</i>

03:41.170 --> 03:42.690
<i>How'd he get that cleared in HQ?</i>

03:42.690 --> 03:44.660
<i>He's aiming at...</i>

03:44.660 --> 03:46.120
Move, Pops!

03:47.790 --> 03:48.940
Well done.

03:48.940 --> 03:49.660
Sir!

03:49.660 --> 03:52.620
We'll meet again on the 
other side of the sky.

03:53.550 --> 03:54.580
<i>Isn't he...?</i>

03:57.090 --> 03:59.170
Shit! Is this for real?!

03:59.170 --> 04:00.590
What's the big idea?!

04:01.280 --> 04:01.720
Stop it—

04:05.080 --> 04:08.380
Hey, Iwa-san! What the hell is going on?!

04:08.800 --> 04:11.730
Pops, Yatsu, go after 
Senior Commissioner Habaki!

04:15.650 --> 04:16.430
Arase! Hey!

04:16.900 --> 04:18.050
These guys are still here?!

04:18.050 --> 04:20.360
This is it, then.

04:20.360 --> 04:26.140
I do not wish to burn the just.

04:26.140 --> 04:26.880
Huh?

04:26.880 --> 04:27.780
Where am I?

04:27.780 --> 04:30.050
Hey! Why am I under arrest?!

04:28.880 --> 04:30.040
What the...?

04:30.040 --> 04:31.250
Ow!

04:31.870 --> 04:33.960
<i>This seems similar.</i>

04:36.790 --> 04:41.070
I heard about it, but don't 
tell me that's the answer.

04:41.070 --> 04:42.760
Did you figure something out?

04:43.140 --> 04:45.980
The Fire-Breathing Bug is 
one person, but they also aren't.

04:45.980 --> 04:48.510
It's a little hard to swallow,

04:48.510 --> 04:51.720
but are we dealing with hypnosis?

04:53.980 --> 04:56.050
Let's split up and search.

04:56.050 --> 04:57.270
You got it.

04:57.690 --> 05:01.230
Oh, crap. What's Kochou 
gonna say to me later?

05:11.960 --> 05:15.280
I... I know this is the right place.

05:15.280 --> 05:16.690
Hi there, Habaki.

05:17.330 --> 05:19.230
Oh! Oh!

05:19.230 --> 05:22.090
I can't believe you're really here!

05:22.090 --> 05:24.110
When did you reach Japan?!

05:24.110 --> 05:25.630
I just got in today.

05:26.110 --> 05:31.350
I was looking for a hotel when I heard 
you made an emergency call to HQ.

05:31.350 --> 05:34.240
Oh, I am unworthy.

05:34.240 --> 05:35.620
That blackout...

05:35.620 --> 05:38.420
Did you use your powers for <i>me</i>?!

05:38.420 --> 05:40.940
You needn't thank me.

05:41.440 --> 05:45.930
Good work, past and future, 
deserves a reward.

05:46.430 --> 05:50.950
Speaking of which, you've given a lot 
to the organization, haven't you?

05:51.210 --> 05:55.430
What that lab called experiments 
were basically just slaughter.

05:55.430 --> 06:00.310
I doubt anyone else would have 
given them his own daughter.

06:00.310 --> 06:01.960
You honor me!

06:01.960 --> 06:06.130
My daughter must be rejoicing 
in the hereafter!

06:06.130 --> 06:07.330
Hmm...

06:07.910 --> 06:11.350
Habaki, you have two things wrong.

06:11.350 --> 06:12.340
What?

06:12.340 --> 06:16.470
"Good work, past and future, 
deserves a reward."

06:16.470 --> 06:18.410
That wasn't about you.

06:19.380 --> 06:21.060
I don't understand.

06:21.060 --> 06:22.310
I told you

06:22.570 --> 06:25.650
that you needn't thank me

06:26.340 --> 06:28.930
because I fully intend to abandon you.

06:28.930 --> 06:29.860
Huh?

06:29.860 --> 06:33.330
That brings us to 
misunderstanding number two.

06:33.820 --> 06:35.670
Isn't "in the hereafter"

06:35.670 --> 06:38.750
something you say about dead people?

06:41.260 --> 06:44.390
Long time no see, Dad.

06:45.260 --> 06:47.240
I-I-It can't be.

06:47.240 --> 06:49.690
Are you... Soara?

06:49.690 --> 06:52.970
That's right. Soara Habaki-chan.

06:53.840 --> 06:57.360
The daughter you gave to the 
Bastard Children of Sabaramond.

06:58.200 --> 07:02.940
Or rather, the troublesome 
love child you disposed of.

07:03.330 --> 07:06.250
I never told you because you 
never tried to find out,

07:06.590 --> 07:11.080
but your daughter became the 
experiments' first survivor.

07:11.080 --> 07:12.410
Congratulations.

07:14.070 --> 07:16.570
Her code name is "Arahabaki."

07:16.570 --> 07:19.080
She outranks you now,

07:19.420 --> 07:21.870
and she asked me

07:22.600 --> 07:27.340
to let her personally execute the 
father who made her a lab rat.

07:27.340 --> 07:28.280
What?!

07:28.280 --> 07:31.160
I've been thinkin' about you all this time,

07:31.160 --> 07:32.630
<i>Father</i>.

07:32.630 --> 07:33.860
W-Wait.

07:33.860 --> 07:39.220
About how I'm gonna cut you 
up everywhere they cut me!

07:39.220 --> 07:41.480
D-Damn you!

07:47.630 --> 07:51.140
Aren't family reunions moving?

07:51.530 --> 07:52.280
Hmm?

07:52.810 --> 07:54.490
Hey, Lulu.

07:56.750 --> 07:59.200
What's the matter, Father?

07:59.200 --> 08:01.520
This is nothing

08:01.520 --> 08:05.630
compared to my decade of agony!

08:05.630 --> 08:09.130
You know, I decided

08:09.750 --> 08:15.970
that if you came to find out 
what happened to me, even once,

08:17.670 --> 08:20.810
I'd at least let you live.

08:21.050 --> 08:23.770
Lucky for me, you're heartless.

08:26.450 --> 08:28.680
So, that's today's target?

08:28.680 --> 08:29.690
Yeah.

08:29.690 --> 08:33.060
I... I still have more to 
offer the organization!

08:33.060 --> 08:39.160
I'm so close to finding the sorcerer 
from the other side of the sky!

08:39.400 --> 08:41.940
I'm not so sure you could pull it off.

08:41.940 --> 08:43.760
Please, give me another chance!

08:43.760 --> 08:44.870
Hmm...

08:45.110 --> 08:48.490
Only facing forward has 
worked out for you so far,

08:48.870 --> 08:51.440
but you should have paused to look back, too.

08:51.940 --> 08:53.550
Both to Soara-chan,

08:53.550 --> 08:54.570
Huh?

08:54.570 --> 08:56.480
and right in this moment.

08:56.480 --> 08:57.010
What do—

08:58.470 --> 08:59.300
Huh?

09:00.060 --> 09:00.890
Did I hit him?

09:00.890 --> 09:05.020
Dead-on. And we got the okay 
to ignore anyone with him.

09:05.310 --> 09:08.970
Still, this is supposed to 
"test the Horojima's skills"?

09:08.970 --> 09:12.230
All we had to do was shoot 
that beat-up middle-aged guy.

09:12.930 --> 09:17.070
Why do you think the Shinjuku intermediary 
called this petty revenge?

09:17.570 --> 09:18.820
We're going out.

09:18.820 --> 09:20.450
Get ready, won't you?

09:20.450 --> 09:21.280
Yes, ma'am!

09:23.250 --> 09:25.470
Boss, gimme the order.

09:25.470 --> 09:26.750
Go ahead.

09:27.140 --> 09:29.710
You have three minutes, Arahabaki.

09:29.710 --> 09:31.170
Sicut vis.

09:31.690 --> 09:32.710
Oh, crap.

09:33.050 --> 09:34.080
What's wrong?

09:34.080 --> 09:35.590
We'd better clear out quick.

09:35.590 --> 09:38.430
We'll hide out on a lower floor and—

09:38.430 --> 09:40.890
Hmm? Too late.

09:40.890 --> 09:41.890
Huh?

09:41.890 --> 09:43.100
She came straight here.

09:53.180 --> 09:54.530
Yo!

09:54.530 --> 09:57.800
You Peeping Toms have really done it now!

09:59.580 --> 10:01.240
We're doomed.

10:02.770 --> 10:05.420
This might be it for us.

10:05.420 --> 10:10.460
Hey, come on. I'd only dished out <i>half</i> 
the pain I had planned for him.

10:10.940 --> 10:14.380
You stole my revenge out from under my nose,

10:14.380 --> 10:17.440
so you'd better make it up to me.

10:18.460 --> 10:20.890
Going for the eyes? Nice thinking!

10:23.860 --> 10:25.290
Heave-ho!

10:34.690 --> 10:35.710
Tch.

10:38.010 --> 10:41.700
Hell of a lot of voyeurs you've got there.

10:42.540 --> 10:43.850
I remember you.

10:45.890 --> 10:50.080
Were you watching us? Waiting to 
clean up if things went south?

10:50.480 --> 10:54.230
Clarissa's too smart to 
give newbies free rein.

10:54.230 --> 10:57.530
Ugh. I knew she was a bitch.

10:57.530 --> 10:58.800
Watch it.

10:59.250 --> 11:02.760
But we owe her one, so... thanks.

11:02.970 --> 11:04.220
Adorable.

11:04.220 --> 11:05.600
She's cute as hell.

11:07.790 --> 11:11.060
Don't think I'll let you off the 
hook just 'cause you're cute!

11:11.330 --> 11:14.520
I've got cute girls on my side, too!

11:14.520 --> 11:16.320
Huh? What the—?!

11:16.810 --> 11:18.740
Where'd the boss go?!

11:18.740 --> 11:21.280
Wait! Are my three minutes up?!

11:21.280 --> 11:24.990
Seriously?! Shit!

11:26.000 --> 11:27.700
Clarissa-san.

11:27.990 --> 11:30.060
I'm sorry to trouble you so late,

11:30.060 --> 11:33.710
but there's someone I simply must speak to

11:34.390 --> 11:36.460
and I need your powers.

11:37.020 --> 11:38.610
<i>L-Lisa?!</i>

11:43.700 --> 11:45.970
I don't believe we've met.

11:46.590 --> 11:49.560
Sayo Shinoyama-chan, isn't it?

11:49.560 --> 11:51.940
Yes. You've heard of me?

11:52.390 --> 11:54.750
Only that you're related to Polka-kun.

11:54.750 --> 11:56.600
Umm... Clarissa-san.

11:57.400 --> 12:01.860
Sayo-san and Rozan-san 
know about the Corpse God.

12:02.490 --> 12:03.530
I see.

12:04.250 --> 12:07.660
Well, you're free to choose 
how much you tell them,

12:08.300 --> 12:09.520
but be careful.

12:10.010 --> 12:16.080
Someone is after Polka Shinoyama, 
the heir to the family fortune.

12:16.080 --> 12:19.340
If they find out, trouble is sure to follow.

12:21.870 --> 12:23.030
<i>What is it?</i>

12:23.030 --> 12:28.100
<i>The intermediary is in contact with 
Polka Shinoyama and your sister, sir.</i>

12:28.320 --> 12:29.930
<i>Stand by for now,</i>

12:30.400 --> 12:33.690
<i>but don't wait for orders if things
 threaten to turn violent.</i>

12:34.050 --> 12:35.100
As you wish.

12:36.490 --> 12:38.060
Lisa Kuraki.

12:38.840 --> 12:39.990
What a nuisance.

12:41.610 --> 12:42.980
I'll be careful.

12:42.980 --> 12:45.990
Well, in that case, you won't 
mind if I tell you here.

12:46.460 --> 12:49.270
Polka-kun—or rather, Corpse God,

12:49.650 --> 12:51.690
I'd like to request your services.

12:52.300 --> 12:54.250
Would you come with me?

12:54.250 --> 12:58.500
I don't mind, but I think Takumi-kun 
and the others ran into trouble.

12:58.880 --> 13:01.120
I can't leave Sayo-san alone.

13:01.120 --> 13:03.720
Oh, that shouldn't be a problem.

13:05.430 --> 13:08.200
Young Miss Shinoyama is minding the house.

13:09.090 --> 13:12.520
Keep her safe until my people get back.

13:13.850 --> 13:15.110
She-fox.

13:16.960 --> 13:19.270
Solitaire snuck in unimpeded.

13:19.490 --> 13:23.030
People of unsound mind turned violent.

13:23.030 --> 13:27.320
A gun was fired at a fellow officer 
and then used to commit suicide.

13:28.160 --> 13:34.750
Someone caused a blackout, during which 
both Solitaire and Habaki vanished.

13:35.710 --> 13:39.920
This has not been a day for 
respecting our territory.

13:40.440 --> 13:45.340
Um... Did you always suspect 
Senior Commissioner Habaki, sir?

13:45.340 --> 13:47.970
He wasn't my only suspect,

13:47.970 --> 13:53.850
but I've been certain we had a 
high-ranking mole for some time.

13:54.260 --> 13:57.980
Five years ago, we almost had him,

13:58.200 --> 14:02.740
but then the person closest to the 
truth vanished along with the evidence.

14:03.690 --> 14:05.280
You don't mean...?

14:06.700 --> 14:08.250
Can you see anything?

14:08.590 --> 14:11.950
Yes. Someone newly dead.

14:12.590 --> 14:15.210
I can make them visible, 
only to the people here.

14:15.710 --> 14:17.160
Please do.

14:25.050 --> 14:27.870
You're looking more handsome these days.

14:27.870 --> 14:30.550
Senior Commissioner Habaki, isn't it?

14:31.020 --> 14:32.800
It's been a long time,

14:33.050 --> 14:36.270
but I've finally reached you.

14:36.600 --> 14:38.230
<i>Habaki!</i>

14:38.230 --> 14:44.990
I... I r-r-remember... remember you.

14:45.660 --> 14:52.560
Y-Y-You were the one who made 
Hosorogi's body d-d-disappear.

14:53.930 --> 14:56.130
Yes. My condolences.

14:56.780 --> 15:00.910
"I killed Hosorogi-san out 
of misguided infatuation"

15:00.910 --> 15:03.880
is the scenario I assume 
you were going for.

15:04.200 --> 15:05.450
<i>Habaki.</i>

15:05.450 --> 15:08.470
<i>He was on my list of suspects,</i>

15:08.840 --> 15:11.060
<i>but why is he dead?!</i>

15:11.060 --> 15:12.840
<i>Did Lisa have him killed?!</i>

15:12.840 --> 15:14.800
<i>But why in a place like this?</i>

15:16.440 --> 15:21.840
You didn't hesitate to grind up 
your lover's body, you monster.

15:21.840 --> 15:25.740
Your disgust is the greatest 
compliment I could hope for.

15:26.110 --> 15:28.730
I only have one question for you.

15:29.170 --> 15:32.910
Who told you to order Hosorogi-san's murder?

15:32.910 --> 15:36.390
You think I'd tell you-ou-ou?

15:36.390 --> 15:37.130
Polka-kun.

15:37.130 --> 15:38.240
I'm already working on it.

15:43.630 --> 15:45.550
All... All right.

15:45.550 --> 15:47.550
I'll tell you as a parting gift!

15:47.550 --> 15:48.420
What did you do?

15:48.420 --> 15:51.170
I cast a spell to guide his mental state.

15:51.570 --> 15:57.140
It's a far cry from brainwashing, 
but it stoked his craving for attention.

15:57.770 --> 15:59.430
Yes.

15:59.430 --> 16:01.420
I made an offering!

16:01.420 --> 16:06.650
An offering to the 
Bastard Children of Sabaramond!

16:07.700 --> 16:10.440
You know Sabaramond-san?

16:12.300 --> 16:13.410
That power.

16:13.410 --> 16:16.410
D-Don't tell me you... you're...

16:16.410 --> 16:20.370
the sorcerer from the other side of the sky?!

16:20.650 --> 16:22.530
<i>He was looking for me?!</i>

16:23.330 --> 16:25.990
The great one will recognize me now!

16:25.990 --> 16:30.710
I'll be able to teach my 
foolish daughter a lesson!

16:31.000 --> 16:32.160
Daughter?

16:32.160 --> 16:33.680
Yes. That's right!

16:34.500 --> 16:37.620
Oh! I offered everything to the great one!

16:37.620 --> 16:40.350
Even my daughter!

16:40.350 --> 16:42.490
She should be grateful!

16:42.490 --> 16:46.110
She died for the organization! For me!

16:46.110 --> 16:49.740
But she wants <i>revenge</i> on me?!

16:50.410 --> 16:51.560
<i>What?!</i>

16:51.560 --> 16:54.620
<i>Habaki's memories are in my mind?!</i>

16:55.300 --> 16:57.740
You'll go to a place beyond 
your wildest dreams.

16:58.090 --> 16:59.950
You should be grateful.

17:00.390 --> 17:02.910
<i>They're reaching me through Polka.</i>

17:04.990 --> 17:05.870
<i>Polka?</i>

17:06.530 --> 17:12.710
Spot me a little cash. You're a 
big shot in the empire now, right?

17:06.800 --> 17:09.280
<i>Fragments mixed with Habaki's past.</i>

17:09.280 --> 17:13.630
<i>Are these Polka's—no, the 
Corpse God's—memories?</i>

17:13.630 --> 17:18.340
I hear you made a killing in 
that last war, so come on.

17:18.820 --> 17:23.060
I need to feed your mom and 
your kid siblings, too, y'know?

17:23.320 --> 17:24.060
Come on.

17:25.270 --> 17:29.100
C-Come on. Have a heart.

17:29.100 --> 17:32.230
You might not mind if <i>I</i> starve, 
but you care about <i>them</i>, right?

17:32.500 --> 17:33.690
Come on.

17:42.900 --> 17:43.680
Sorry.

17:44.250 --> 17:50.730
Those guys in Nyanild say they'll 
give me more drugs if I kill you.

17:51.120 --> 17:54.210
If you want to blame someone, blame them.

17:54.570 --> 17:58.190
But why would you hold a grudge, anyway?

17:58.190 --> 17:59.640
It's not just you.

17:59.640 --> 18:02.570
Your mom, your little brother and sister...

18:02.570 --> 18:04.680
I, well, you know,

18:04.970 --> 18:07.490
sold 'em all for a good price.

18:09.020 --> 18:12.610
The whole family helped me 
out until the bitter end.

18:12.610 --> 18:14.150
I appreciate it, you know?

18:16.740 --> 18:17.690
Huh? What?!

18:17.690 --> 18:18.480
What's this?

18:18.480 --> 18:19.610
Clarissa-san,

18:20.640 --> 18:22.780
I'm still calm.

18:23.550 --> 18:28.350
We ought to get more information 
out of him. I know that.

18:28.720 --> 18:29.750
But...

18:30.220 --> 18:32.280
may I do as I please?

18:33.280 --> 18:36.510
Wh-Wh-What are you...?

18:37.120 --> 18:42.850
No one else in <i>this</i> world can play at 
being the grim reaper, Corpse God-kun.

18:43.590 --> 18:45.060
As you will.

18:56.600 --> 18:58.140
Well, dear friend?

18:58.140 --> 19:01.740
As a necromancer, how does it 
feel to become undead yourself?

19:02.580 --> 19:07.260
This cursed object dissolves the 
body to prevent resurrection.

19:07.610 --> 19:12.750
Only the Geldwood Order's rotten saint 
would prepare something like it.

19:13.370 --> 19:16.870
It was also imbued with 
a soul-destroying spell,

19:16.870 --> 19:22.760
but unfortunately for them,
 I didn't raise your soul to be so fragile.

19:23.340 --> 19:29.270
Never forget that I made 
you undead on a whim.

19:29.270 --> 19:32.110
Oh? Do we misremember?

19:32.510 --> 19:36.740
"Thank goodness we finished the soul 
core before his brain broke down."

19:36.740 --> 19:39.280
Those were your words, 
and you sounded relieved.

19:39.440 --> 19:41.440
Your memory is faulty.

19:41.440 --> 19:43.160
Sticking to it?

19:43.370 --> 19:49.090
Then do we misremember you 
begging Utsurojuza for help, too?

19:48.640 --> 19:54.520
<b>Byadian Court Sorcerer 
Third Rank

Utsurojuza</b>

19:48.640 --> 19:54.520
m 0 0 l 290 0 290 80 0 80

19:49.520 --> 19:53.780
He "stored" the poison and curse 
just before they reached the brain.

19:54.570 --> 19:57.380
Your Majesty is entirely mistaken.

19:57.910 --> 20:03.090
You ought to see a healer 
and have your head examined.

20:03.090 --> 20:06.090
Could you get any worse, bewitching old hag?

20:07.460 --> 20:11.600
No one else would call our 
imperial majesty crazy.

20:11.850 --> 20:16.940
Not a kind word for your apprentice, 
<i>and</i> you call His Majesty crazy?

20:16.940 --> 20:18.610
That's as bad as it gets.

20:18.610 --> 20:22.070
Am I wrong? Well, Corpse God?

20:22.300 --> 20:25.960
Now, now, Utsurojuza. Leave it at that.

20:26.540 --> 20:32.080
We are quite sane, but we nearly 
lost our head with worry.

20:32.630 --> 20:36.810
All because you went and got yourself 
stabbed to death, dear friend.

20:38.000 --> 20:39.790
Hm? What's wrong?

20:39.790 --> 20:43.340
Using bones to speak is a hassle.

20:43.690 --> 20:46.300
Still, I get the gist.

20:46.670 --> 20:52.350
He's confused because Your Majesty 
treats him like nothing's changed.

20:52.730 --> 20:57.480
He must have been worried that 
undeath would end your friendship.

20:57.480 --> 20:58.900
Were you really?

20:59.290 --> 21:02.170
Then you severely underestimated.

21:03.040 --> 21:06.110
Oh, we don't mean us.

21:06.540 --> 21:08.530
We mean yourself.

21:08.530 --> 21:12.750
And don't think of taking 
vengeance on your father.

21:12.750 --> 21:16.290
You needn't sully yourself 
for a nobody like him.

21:16.900 --> 21:18.640
Never forget, dear friend.

21:19.380 --> 21:25.200
Whatever you become, we and our 
empire will always stand by you,

21:25.680 --> 21:27.770
Rizdilusia Redrazalf.

21:30.810 --> 21:32.490
Gods don't play games.

21:33.020 --> 21:35.060
I still believe that, even now.

21:37.250 --> 21:39.750
Only immature beings such as myself

21:40.300 --> 21:42.690
toy with lives out of emotion.

21:47.860 --> 21:48.970
Huh?

21:48.970 --> 21:50.830
How many times must we say it?

21:51.280 --> 21:55.040
You needn't sully yourself 
for a nobody like him.

21:56.310 --> 21:59.750
I don't recall summoning you,

22:00.470 --> 22:01.470
Your Imperial Majesty.
